      "Signal 1 — AI Drug Discovery + Refractory Glioblastoma + Cucurbitacin B Natural Product Repurposing + Cell Cycle & DNA Replication / Transcriptomic Response of Glioblastoma Cells to Cucurbitacin B Reveals Alterations in Cell Cycle and DNA Replication: GSE347373 (score 6, n=6, Homo sapiens, Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing, pdat 2026/09/20 = 1 day ago, raw TSV files, watcher query 'OpenFold weights' [query-routing artifact]) is the FRESHEST NOVEL Cucurbitacin-B / CuB / triterpenoid-natural-product / glioblastoma-refractory-cancer / cell-cycle-arrest / DNA-replication-inhibition transcriptomic atlas in the entire 2026-09-22 hits.jsonl. Cucurbitacin B (a tetracyclic-triterpenoid natural product from Cucurbitaceae family — pumpkins, gourds, cucumbers; MW 558.7) is a well-characterized STAT3-pathway inhibitor with demonstrated anti-cancer activity across glioblastoma, melanoma, breast, lung, colorectal, pancreatic, and hepatocellular carcinoma. The KEY mechanism: CuB inhibits STAT3-phosphorylation (pY705) and STAT3-DNA-binding, triggering G2-M-arrest via CDK1/cyclin-B1 downregulation + WEE1 upregulation + ATR-CHK1-mediated replication-stress + γH2AX-formation + caspase-3-activation + PARP-cleavage + BCL2/MCL1-suppression. GBM (WHO-grade-IV-astrocytoma, ~14K-US-cases/year, median-survival-15-months, 5-year-survival-<5%) is the most-aggressive-primary-brain-tumor. Standard-of-care: maximal-safe-resection + radiotherapy + temozolomide-TMZ + tumor-treating-fields-TTF-Optune. Cucurbitacin-B-is-an-ideal-natural-product-repurposing-candidate: existing-preclinical-data-in-multiple-cancers + favorable-safety-profile-from-traditional-medicine-use + STAT3-is-validated-GBM-target + natural-product-formulation-feasibility.",
